# CSS class names

Mandatory. Class names must look human-written, not generated.

## Rules

- Write class names in **simple natural English** (kebab-case).
- **Never** use BEM element separators (`__`). Prefer `panel-header`, not `panel__header`.
- Do not over-engineer names. Keep them short and obvious.
- Modifiers with a hyphenated suffix are fine: `home-panel-animated`, `alert-card-unread`.
- Match nearby naming in the file before inventing a new pattern.

## Examples

| Incorrect | Correct |
|---|---|
| `home-panel__header` | `home-panel-header` |
| `alert-card__meta` | `alert-card-meta` |
| `table-header-row__title-col` | `table-header-title` |

## In SCSS

Do not nest with `&__child`. Use a flat name or `&-child` (no `__` in the output):

```scss
// Incorrect
.home-panel {
  &__header { ... }
}

// Correct
.home-panel-header { ... }
```
